        "id": 85978,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-15T20:41:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"metaphysician\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/edb3f5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> metaphysician:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If you've got a good hand to use with Arc of Power, are you really going to <em>need</em> more than one turn of protection?&nbsp; The right four cards from Tempest in a single turn could completely change the course of a game in a definitive manner ( think \"Shackles, Ball Lightning, Lightning Blade, Chain Lightning\", or something thereabouts ).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I agree; after Prime Warden Tempest does something like this he doesn't have any cards left to play, anyway. A well-timed heroic interception would be perfect.</p>",
